@startuml server_release_unhappy
title MongoDB Server (mongo / SERVER) — Release (Unhappy Paths)

skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FBE9E7
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #C0392B
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F5F5F5

' Lane order is set by first appearance: declare CI first so it renders on the
' left, matching the happy-path diagram.
|CI|
|Human|
start

:RC built **rX.Y.Z-rcN** (tag-triggered Evergreen build);
:**test the RC** (correctness / perf / multiversion);

' Comment 6: reworded gate
if (verified: no frightening build failures\nAND critical fixes complete?) then (yes)
  :promote to GA -> see happy-path diagram;
  stop
else (no — RC not ready)
endif

' Comment 10: an RC commonly fails for ordinary (non-emergency) reasons.
' That just means land the fix and re-spin. It is NOT EOL patching.
:land the fix (tracked in SERVER; release work in STAR)
if the fix must also reach other SUPPORTED release lines,
back-port it (backport skill: per-version PR + Evergreen patch,
Jira BACKPORT; may update etc/backports_required_for_multiversion_tests.yml);

:**RE-SPIN** -> tag **rX.Y.Z-rc(N+1)**
new tag re-triggers the release build
skip_existing (=is_release) means a re-spin NEVER
overwrites already-shipped artifacts in push_bucket;
note right: loop back to "test the RC"\nuntil the RC is ready
stop

' ── separate rare/failure outcomes ─────────────────────
' These are independent scenarios, not branches of the RC loop above, so each
' gets its own start. (A split/split again block would imply they fan out from
' the re-spin flow, and its empty first branch rendered as a detached group.)

' Comment 10: EOL patching is emergency-only (operational policy,
' not encoded in the mongo repo).
|Human|
start
partition "EMERGENCY EOL PATCH (rare)" {
  :patch an EOL / older line (e.g. v4.4)
  ONLY during an emergency response
  (distinct from a normal RC re-spin);
  stop
}

' Comment 11: GA sometimes has to be abandoned.
|Human|
start
partition "GA ABANDONED" {
  :GA fails to build, OR issue found during Atlas rollout;
  :withhold from **OM / CM** and **Downloads**
  -> do NOT mirror to public; respin a later version;
  stop
}

' Comment 12: Copybara mirror safety (public push).
|CI|
start
partition "PUBLIC MIRROR BLOCKED (Copybara safety checks)" {
  if (fast-forward only · correct Evergreen project (master) ·\nnot moving public branch backward?) then (ok)
    :advance public branch, then publish tag
    -> mongodb/mongo;
    stop
  else (blocked)
    :task FAILS — refuses to move public branch backward
    (or tag already points elsewhere) -> NO public push
    re-running is a no-op once destination reached the target;
    stop
  endif
}

@enduml
